BALAJI>YANI: a chemistry set. (Counterpart to magic marker, for
BALAJI>potions instead of scrolls.) Apply it to make any already IDed
BALAJI>potion. Heavy, not rechargeable, mega-useful potions like GL
BALAJI>use up many charges.

I *like* it. Maybe healers and wizards get bonuses using them and/or
they can start out with them. To create a potion, you must have the
kit *and* a potion of water (its blessed/cursed status determines the
status of the potion produced). The odds of producing the desired
potion, however, should be low to preserve the game balance.

Maybe it should be a requirement that a potion is quaffed (not merely
identified) before the chemistry set can be used to recreate it. Or,
conversely, a potion *must* have been magically identified to
determine the proper mix of reagents from the kit.

